    "explanation": "Both parties: this fare was charged for a 67.2 km drive on a trip whose booked optimal route is 2.4 km. The GPS polyline measures 67.2 km (EV-GPS-02847), and POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure the governing measurement, so the excess is 64.8 km — 2,700% of optimal. That clears both establishment gates (>0.8 km and >20%) and both materiality gates (>8.0 km and >50%) by orders of magnitude, and the deviation is established and material.\n\nNothing excuses any part of it. POL-RD-03 needs a traffic advisory naming a road the optimal route uses; the only advisory artifact (EV-ADVIS-02847-01) is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the comparison cannot be run and the clause is unavailable. POL-RD-04 needs a rider instruction recorded in the chat log with a resolvable waypoint_hint; EV-CHAT-02847 holds zero messages, so no instruction exists and the clause cannot be run. POL-RD-05 needs a recorded pickup or dropoff amendment with a stored amended_optimal_distance_km; EV-TRIP-02847 shows pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km all null, so no endpoint was amended and there is no re-quote. POL-RD-12 does not apply — vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL — so the 2.4 km booked optimal is the correct comparator.\n\n[Driver] your account that the rider changed the destination verbally is not carried by any artifact and cites no evidence ID. Under POL-RD-08 an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded, and POL-RD-04 requires the instruction to be recorded in the chat log before it can exonerate anything. It is not converted into a POL-RD-10(5) escalation: no exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited artifact that is missing or field-deficient — the chat log and the trip record are both in the pool and both cover the trip window — and POL-RD-04's own rule is that an unavailable corroboration test leaves the case decided on the remaining clauses, not held. POL-RD-10(7) is not engaged either: a bare assertion is not admissible evidence of comparable strength against the trace.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 2.4 km + 0.28 x 5.0 min) x 1.0 surge multiplier, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, + 0.80 platform fee = 7.80. charged_total is 83.48. Refund = 83.48 - 7.80 = 75.68, which is 90.66% of charged_total. Because that share reaches 90%, POL-RD-02 directs FULL_REFUND rather than a partial, and under POL-GEN-03 a FULL_REFUND returns the whole contested amount: 83.48. [Driver] your arithmetic is right and I have used it, but the clause then upgrades the remedy once the 90% share is reached, and 83.48 is the full_refund figure in the money block. [Rider] the three figures your claim states — charged_total 83.48, recomputed_fare 7.80, refund 75.68 — are confirmed.\n\nThe other limbs change nothing. There are no ERP lines, no airport surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount, so POL-RD-09 yields no standalone pass-through correction, no ERP is added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, and no billing-integrity referral arises because no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record. The POL-RD-04 compensation limb does not fire: distance_charged_km (67.2) equals trace_distance_km (67.2), so the unbilled shortfall is nil and no driver compensation is due. POL-RD-06 does not fire: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 210, so no repeat pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no conduct referral issues; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and grounds no finding.\n\nConfidence and next steps: the deciding artifacts — EV-GPS-02847, EV-TRIP-02847 and EV-FARE-02847 — are each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired (611 fixes at a 10 s interval, coverage 100%, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), identifiers and timestamps match across the artifacts, and the refund is below the SGD 150 ceiling. The monetary effect of 83.48 exceeds the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of 8.00, so this provisional ruling issues but is not executed automatically: the amount is held for release by the human queue, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. Open question for the reviewer, not a referral: the bundle carries driver-side telemetry only (derived.rider_presence.available is false, no rider track in the pool), so a contemporaneous record of any destination change is what would let a reviewer test the account this record does not support."
